                "text": "<p>My parents are from Tamil Nadu, the southernmost state in India. We drink filter coffee. Where I grew up, chai was spoken about as a North Indian thing — someone else's drink.</p><p>What I did grow up with was the complaint. Everyone around me agreed that the chai in American coffee shops was nothing like the real thing. I knew it. It just never occurred to me that it was mine to fix.</p>",
